When we want to find $D^{-1}$, and then calculate $A = D^{-1}B$, we will use row reduction. Row reduce $A:\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 6\\ 0 & 33 \end{pmatrix}$ , and we get:
\begin{align*}
\begin{pmatrix} 
           1   & 6\\
           7  & -3
           \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}
Then find the inverse, and we get
\begin{align*}
D^{-1}B =
\frac{1}{33}\begin{pmatrix} 
           6 & 6\\
           7  & 1
           \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}
Finally, you can use a calculator or just do matrix multiplication to check that this works:
